--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/calm-terminal-badge-polling.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+---
+"@jmfederico/pi-web": patch
+---
+
+Refresh the Terminal workspace badge every ten seconds instead of every second. The badge count can now be up to ten seconds stale, which cuts background requests to the session daemon by ten times; an open Terminal panel is unaffected because it stays live over its own connection.
diff --git a/.changeset/quiet-browser-resume-refresh.md b/.changeset/quiet-browser-resume-refresh.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ffb82ecf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/quiet-browser-resume-refresh.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+---
+"@jmfederico/pi-web": patch
+---
+
+Stop the burst of background requests PI WEB used to send every time the browser tab regained focus. Returning to a tab can raise several resume signals at once, and each one started a full refresh that opened a fresh connection per request; bursts are now collapsed into a single refresh that runs a few requests at a time. Transient network failures on those reads also retry once after a spread-out delay instead of failing loudly, which removes the "NetworkError when attempting to fetch resource" and "Plugin backend request unavailable" errors seen mainly in Firefox.
